This folder holds the parts that must exist before Flux can work. Flux does
not manage them. You deploy them by hand.

- ccmd, netd, loadbalancerd: deployed together from this folder.
- flux: the Flux controllers.
- git: the notification objects and the token. Apply this after flux. The
  token file is a template: fill it in before you apply, and never commit a
  filled copy.

On main, the images built in this repo use the latest tag. A release branch
has the real tags.

Deploy ccmd, netd and loadbalancerd together, from a release branch:

kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//deploy/base/release?ref=release/<tag>

New cluster? Run in this order:

kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//deploy/base/release?ref=release/<tag>
kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//deploy/base/flux?ref=release/<tag>
kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//deploy/base/git?ref=release/<tag>
kubectl apply -k https://github.com/teapotovh/teapot//deploy/release?ref=release/<tag>
